    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0116",
      "sequence": 128,
      "meaning": "There is no real difference between the qualified and qualityless, so sages, Purāṇas, wise people and Vedas sing. The qualityless, formless, unseen and unborn One becomes qualified under devotees’ love. How can what is without qualities become qualified? As water and hail are not essentially different. How could delusion be ascribed to the One whose name is the sun consuming confusion’s darkness? Rāma is the sun of being-consciousness-bliss; there is not the slightest night of delusion in him. Bhagavān is naturally self-luminous, so no dawn of realization is needed there. Joy and sorrow, knowledge and ignorance, egoity and pride are properties of the individual creature; Rāma is Brahman, all-pervading, ancient, supreme bliss and Lord beyond all, famed as the cosmic Person, treasury of light and manifest master of higher and lower. Calling that jewel of Raghu’s line his own Lord, Śiva bows his head.",
