      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0119",
      "sequence": 131,
      "meaning": "Śiva says that by the power of Rāma’s name he grants freedom from grief to beings he sees dying in Kāśī. That very Raghubara is his Lord, master of all moving and unmoving beings and knower within every heart. Even helplessly uttering his name burns sins accumulated over many births; those who remember it reverently cross becoming’s ocean as though it were a cow’s hoofprint. Rāma is that supreme Self, so Pārvatī’s speech bringing intense doubt there was ill-suited and would carry away knowledge, detachment and every virtue. Hearing Śiva’s doubt-destroying words, the whole structure of false reasoning dissolves. Love and trust in Raghupati’s feet arise and painful disbelief passes. Again and again Girijā grasps the Lord’s lotus feet, joins her lotus hands and speaks excellent words steeped in love’s nectar.",
